{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["<b>I, I.</b> Twice, like אנכי אנכי, or כי אני הוא ולא אשנה, and this is the correct reading, for there is no verb with [the first] אני. [The meaning is:] \"I am he who put Israel to death, and I will give them life\" — and behold, they were not delivered; and \"there is none who delivers from my hand\" — \"even you [are] from my hand, until I execute judgment upon you.\" And many say that from this verse we learn [about] the life of the World to Come, and the proof is that he said first אמית and afterward אחיה, and likewise ה' ממית ומחיה, and the proof [is] ה' מוריד שאול ויעל. And others said [the proof is] from the verse ואך את דמכם לנפשותיכם, and likewise וצדקה תהיה לנו — \"for it is your life\" in the World to Come and \"and length of your days\" in this world — למען ייטב לך. And our master Hai, of blessed memory, said that Scripture had no need to explain the matter of the World to Come, for it was known through translation. And in my opinion, the Torah was given to all, not to one alone, and the matter of the World to Come, not one in a thousand will understand it, for it is deep; and the reward of the World to Come depends on the matter of the soul. Now, it [the World to Come] takes the place of the service of the heart, and its service is to contemplate the deeds of HaShem, for they are the ladder upon which to ascend to the level of knowledge of HaShem, which is the essence. And behold, the Torah too explained to the discerning the matter of the Tree of Life; and behold, there is power to overcome the cherubim, and one who eats of the Tree of Life lives forever, like the ministering angels. And likewise in the psalm of the sons of Korah: שמעו זאת כל העמים — and the secret [is in] אך אלהים יפדה נפשי מיד שאול כי יקחני סלה, and likewise אחר כבוד תקחני — and behold, both have לקיחה, as with the matter of Enoch and Elijah. And after he said ויקר פדיון נפשם, how did he say יפדה נפשי? And the discerning will understand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "Resolved הגאון/רבינו האי as R. Hai Gaon by inference from the epithet and context. The phrase 'והוא הנכון כי אין עמו פועל' is read as: the correct reading is that there is no verb paired with the first אני, i.e., the doubled pronoun stands alone without a verb."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:21.450659006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}